(From: n.okafor@riverside-oncology.example) Tj T*
(To: complaints@aivoa-pharma.example) Tj T*
(Date: 2026-07-18) Tj T*
(Subject: Visible particles in Onkovex 100 mg/10 ml injection - batch OVX-26042) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Dear Sir or Madam,) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(I am a senior nurse in the oncology day unit at Riverside Oncology Centre. Today, while) Tj T*
(preparing an infusion, I inspected a vial of Onkovex 100 mg/10 ml Solution for Injection) Tj T*
(\(batch OVX-26042, expiry 2027-04-30\) against a light box and saw several small floating) Tj T*
(particles, grey and fibre-like, in the solution. The vial was within expiry, the flip-) Tj T*
(off cap) Tj T*
(and the stopper were intact, and there was no discoloration of the liquid.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(We inspected the remaining vials from the same carton and found visible particles in 2) Tj T*
(of the) Tj T*
(10 vials. All 10 vials have been withdrawn from use and are stored at 2-8 degrees) Tj T*
(Celsius as) Tj T*
(per the label, in a monitored fridge with no recorded temperature excursion.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(No product from these vials was administered to any patient, so there is no adverse) Tj T*
(event to) Tj T*
(report at this time.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Given that this is a sterile parenteral product used in immunocompromised patients, we) Tj T*
(would) Tj T*
(like confirmation of the sterility status of this batch and information on whether other) Tj T*
(units) Tj T*
(have been affected.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Yours faithfully,) Tj T*
(Nnamdi Okafor) Tj T*
(Senior Oncology Nurse, Riverside Oncology Centre) Tj T*
(Tel: +44 161 496 0345) Tj T*
